Outdoor luminaires and lighting systems existing prior to the effective date of this ordinance are protected and may continue as nonconforming structures or uses. When nonconforming luminaires are replaced with new luminaires or when nonconforming lighting systems are expanded or extended, such replacement, expansion or extension shall be done in accordance with all applicable provisions of this chapter. Nonconforming luminaires and lighting systems may be maintained and repaired. Maintenance and repair means:

a. Replacement of burned out or inoperative lamps;

b. Replacement or repair of damaged or inoperative luminaire components like ballasts, ignitors, lenses, reflectors, refractors, sockets, or photocell controls.

